Specifically, we replace absolute positional embeddings with Rotary Positional Embeddings (RoPE)
[37], which improve extrapolation to longer contexts and reduce parameter count. Furthermore, we
adopt the SwiGLU activation function in the MLP blocks, which has been shown to outperform
standard GELU or ReLU in both convergence and downstream performance [33]. To further simplify
the architecture and enhance training stability, we substitute standard LayerNorm with RMSNorm
and eliminate all bias terms. These design choices are consistent with [3, 40].



